    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160">

                <pb facs="0167" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg93"/>

                <head>Mr. Adderly to Mr. Layard</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thirty-five, Eutin
                            Place,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 17, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Layard</hi>: I enclose a letter to the man
                    in the federal army of whom I spoke to you, which you were so good as to say you
                    would have forwarded.</p>
                <p>His parents are ready to give any sum up to £50 for his discharge, which I will
                    guarantee. The man received $300 on the 2d of March, 1864, as half of his
                    bounty-money, and $13 a month’s pay ever since.</p>
                <p>He enlisted for three years. His address is as on the enclosed letter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. B. ADDERLY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>A. H. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Layard,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
